---
import AdminShell from '../../components/AdminShell.astro';
---
<AdminShell title="Documentation" eyebrow="Knowledge Base" description="Current CajunSites operating standards, architecture, workflows, controls, and improvement priorities." active="documentation">
  <style>
    .doc-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:260px minmax(0,1fr);gap:18px;align-items:start}.toc{position:sticky;top:86px;max-height:calc(100vh - 112px);overflow:auto}.toc h3{margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--purple-950)}.toc a{display:block;padding:8px 10px;border-radius:9px;text-decoration:none;color:#554b5c;font-size:.84rem;font-weight:700}.toc a:hover{background:#f5eff9;color:var(--purple-800)}.docs{display:grid;gap:16px}.doc{scroll-margin-top:90px}.doc h2{font-size:1.45rem;letter-spacing:-.025em;color:var(--purple-950);margin:0 0 12px}.doc h3{font-size:1rem;color:var(--purple-900);margin:20px 0 8px}.doc p,.doc li{font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65}.doc ul,.doc ol{margin:8px 0 0;padding-left:22px}.doc code{font-size:.82rem;background:#f5f1f7;border:1px solid #ebe3ee;border-radius:6px;padding:2px 6px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.doc table{width:100%;border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;margin-top:10px}.doc th,.doc td{text-align:left;padding:10px 11px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-right:0;border-bottom:0;font-size:.84rem;vertical-align:top}.doc tr>*:last-child{border-right:1px solid var(--line)}.doc tr:last-child>*{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.doc th{background:#fbf9fc;color:#554b5c}.callout{border-left:4px solid var(--gold-500);background:#fff9e8;padding:13px 15px;border-radius:10px;margin-top:12px;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.55}.callout.red{border-left-color:#b73030;background:#fff3f3}.callout.green{border-left-color:#178a47;background:#f0fbf4}.status-flow{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:7px;margin-top:10px}.status-flow span{background:#f2edf7;color:var(--purple-800);padding:6px 9px;border-radius:999px;font-size:.76rem;font-weight:800}.search{margin-bottom:16px;position:sticky;top:80px;z-index:10}.search input{width:100%;min-height:44px;padding:0 13px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.96);box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(34,6,63,.04)}.priority-table td:first-child{font-weight:850}.priority-p0{color:#9b2424}.priority-p1{color:#7b5100}.priority-p2{color:#4f5964}@media(max-width:900px){.doc-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}.toc{position:static;max-height:none}.toc-links{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.doc table{display:block;overflow:auto}.search{position:static}}@media(max-width:620px){.toc-links{grid-template-columns:1fr}.doc{padding:16px}.doc h2{font-size:1.28rem}}
  </style>

  <div class="search"><input id="docSearch" type="search" placeholder="Search CajunSites documentation..." aria-label="Search documentation" /></div>
  <div class="doc-layout">
    <aside class="admin-card toc">
      <h3>Contents</h3>
      <div class="toc-links">
        <a href="#health">Current Project Health</a>
        <a href="#business">Business Overview</a>
        <a href="#offer">Offer & Scope</a>
        <a href="#sales">Sales & Qualification</a>
        <a href="#prospects">Prospect Workflow</a>
        <a href="#concept-factory">Concept Factory</a>
        <a href="#conversion">Prospect Conversion</a>
        <a href="#lifecycle">Customer Lifecycle</a>
        <a href="#build-standard">Production Build Standard</a>
        <a href="#seo">SEO Standard</a>
        <a href="#maintenance">Maintenance Standard</a>
        <a href="#architecture">Technical Architecture</a>
        <a href="#payments">Payments & Billing</a>
        <a href="#onboarding">Onboarding Automation</a>
        <a href="#dashboard">Dashboard Operations</a>
        <a href="#security">Security & Data Handling</a>
        <a href="#database">Database & Migrations</a>
        <a href="#deployment">Deployment & CI</a>
        <a href="#qa">QA Checklist</a>
        <a href="#incident">Incident & Recovery</a>
        <a href="#legal">Legal & Tax Notes</a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <section class="docs" id="docs">
      <article class="admin-card doc" id="health" data-doc>
        <h2>Current Project Health & Improvement Priorities</h2>
        <p>CajunSites has a functioning public site, checkout/onboarding automation, D1 operations layer, internal dashboard, prospect pipeline, business research, automated concept generation, prospect cleanup, and prospect-to-customer conversion. The platform is suitable for controlled sales validation, with the following hardening priorities before significant volume.</p>
        <table class="priority-table"><thead><tr><th>Priority</th><th>Area</th><th>Current Direction</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td class="priority-p0">P0</td><td>Admin access</td><td>Protect <code>/admin/*</code> at the server or Cloudflare Access layer. The current static pages use a client login overlay while API data is server-protected.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="priority-p0">P0</td><td>Internal passwords</td><td>Login now accepts both the current HMAC format and PBKDF2 records created by user-management actions. Move to one explicit versioned scheme and a dedicated password pepper.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="priority-p1">P1</td><td>Billing state</td><td>Add recurring payment failure, recovery, subscription cancellation, and refund synchronization from Stripe.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="priority-p1">P1</td><td>Concept factory</td><td>Move multi-signal classification into the core factory for every visual family, not only specialized intercepts such as Car Wash.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="priority-p1">P1</td><td>Database</td><td>Create a complete canonical migration history and remove request-time schema mutation and runtime prospect seeding.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="priority-p2">P2</td><td>Dashboard</td><td>Add prospect KPIs, Stripe-backed financial metrics, live platform health, better error states, and mobile sign-out.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="priority-p2">P2</td><td>CI</td><td>Worker JavaScript syntax checking is now part of CI. Add Worker bundle validation and behavior tests next.</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <div class="callout">The detailed source-controlled audit is <code>docs/PROJECT-AUDIT-2026-09-11.md</code>. Treat this section as the dashboard summary of that audit.</div>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="business" data-doc>
        <h2>Business Overview</h2>
        <p><strong>CajunSites</strong> provides standardized, professionally designed websites for small businesses at a clear fixed price. Independent Holdings, LLC operates the CajunSites brand.</p>
        <table><tbody><tr><th>Brand</th><td>CajunSites</td></tr><tr><th>Tagline</th><td>Websites Built for Small Business</td></tr><tr><th>Primary message</th><td>A professional website. Without the agency price.</td></tr><tr><th>Primary domain</th><td>cajunsites.com</td></tr><tr><th>Primary contact</th><td>hello@cajunsites.com</td></tr></tbody></table>
        <div class="callout">AI is an internal production advantage. Do not market CajunSites as an “AI website” company.</div>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="offer" data-doc>
        <h2>Offer & Scope</h2>
        <table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Price</th><th>Included</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Website Design & Launch</td><td>$499 one time</td><td>Up to 5 pages, responsive design, contact or quote form, maps/location as applicable, local SEO foundation, domain connection, SSL, and production launch.</td></tr><tr><td>Hosting & Maintenance</td><td>$49/month</td><td>Hosting, SSL, platform maintenance, routine content changes, form support, basic troubleshooting, and recovery as applicable.</td></tr></tbody></table>
        <h3>Standard Pages</h3><p>Home, Services, About, Reviews, Contact.</p>
        <h3>Outside Base Scope</h3><p>Ecommerce, custom software, advanced integrations, major redesigns, ongoing SEO campaigns, link building, monthly content creation, ongoing Google Business Profile management, and customer email hosting/administration.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="sales" data-doc>
        <h2>Sales & Qualification</h2>
        <p>Primary motion: identify a qualified business, generate a personalized concept, contact the owner, show the concept, then close the $499 launch plus $49/month service.</p>
        <h3>Website Gate</h3><p>A prospect is disqualified if its Google Business Profile contains any Website button or URL, including Facebook, Fresha, Square, Booksy, NAPA, corporate sites, old sites, or poor sites.</p>
        <h3>Preferred Prospect</h3><ul><li>Owner-operated local service business</li><li>Established Google Business Profile</li><li>Strong public reviews</li><li>No website listed in Google</li><li>Clear services and market area</li><li>Reachable owner or decision maker</li></ul>
        <h3>Approved Cold Call Direction</h3><p>“I noticed your business doesn’t have a website, so we mocked one up for you. There’s no charge or obligation. Can I text you the preview?”</p>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="prospects" data-doc>
        <h2>Prospect Workflow</h2>
        <div class="status-flow"><span>Qualified</span><span>Concept Built</span><span>Contacted</span><span>Concept Viewed</span><span>Won</span><span>Lost</span></div>
        <p>Prospect records contain business identity, qualification, website gate, contact details, outreach history, concept state, research data, follow-up, outcome, conversion linkage, and internal notes.</p>
        <h3>Removal Standard</h3><p>Owner/Admin prospect removal is destructive. If a concept exists, CajunSites must remove the Vercel project domain, stored concept deployment, and CajunSites DNS record before deleting the D1 prospect row. Cleanup is fail-closed. A prospect linked to a customer cannot be deleted from the prospect pipeline.</p>
        <div class="callout green">Unbuilt prospects can be deleted without Vercel/DNS cleanup. Built concepts require the relevant cleanup credentials and successful asset cleanup first.</div>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="concept-factory" data-doc>
        <h2>Concept Factory</h2>
        <p>Concept sites are personalized sales previews, not final production websites. Build Concept can automatically research the business, generate a static concept, deploy it to the shared Vercel concept project, create the CajunSites CNAME, register the Vercel domain, assign the alias, then store the deployment state in D1.</p>
        <h3>Research Inputs</h3><p>Research uses current public sources and stores a vertical, factual summary, verified facts, verified services, review themes, suggested sections, and source links. Unsupported claims must be omitted.</p>
        <h3>Visual Classification</h3><p>The preferred classifier combines researched vertical, prospect category, verified services, and suggested sections. Car Wash currently uses this multi-signal path. The remaining base visual families still need to be moved to the same shared classifier.</p>
        <h3>Current Visual Families</h3><ul><li>Car Wash / Auto Care</li><li>Collision / Auto Body</li><li>Auto Repair / Diesel</li><li>Towing / Roadside</li><li>Plumbing</li><li>Cleaning</li><li>Beauty / Salon / Wellness</li><li>Childcare / Learning</li><li>Floral</li><li>Generic Local Business fallback</li></ul>
        <h3>Concept Guardrails</h3><ul><li>Never invent years in business, licenses, insurance, certifications, awards, services, guarantees, testimonials, service areas, or 24/7 availability.</li><li>Representative imagery must match the vertical and must not imply the pictured people, vehicles, property, work, awards, or credentials belong to the prospect.</li><li>Concept pages remain <code>noindex,nofollow</code>.</li><li>Generic fallback should become an explicit visible warning rather than a silent default.</li><li>Rebuilds should eventually delete or track the prior Vercel deployment so old deployments do not accumulate.</li></ul>
        <div class="callout">Improvement target: one core visual-family registry with multi-signal classification, image pools, deterministic variants, research-confidence gating, image validation, and stored build metadata.</div>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="conversion" data-doc>
        <h2>Prospect to Customer Conversion</h2>
        <p>Convert to Customer opens the standard Stripe Payment Link using <code>client_reference_id=prospect_&lt;id&gt;</code> and prefills email when available. After a verified paid checkout, the customer is linked back to the source prospect, the prospect moves to Won, the concept URL can be copied into customer site metadata, and Activity records the conversion.</p>
        <div class="callout red">Known hardening item: prospect conversion finalization currently occurs after the base webhook handler succeeds. Conversion-linking failures must become retryable through webhook failure or durable reconciliation so a paid customer cannot remain permanently unlinked.</div>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="lifecycle" data-doc>
        <h2>Customer Lifecycle</h2>
        <div class="status-flow"><span>Paid - Awaiting Onboarding</span><span>Onboarding Received</span><span>Waiting on Customer</span><span>Ready to Build</span><span>Building</span><span>Internal QA</span><span>Customer Review</span><span>Revisions</span><span>Approved for Launch</span><span>Launching</span><span>Live</span><span>Active Customer</span></div>
        <p>Exception statuses are <strong>Payment Issue</strong> and <strong>Cancelled</strong>. Stripe lifecycle synchronization should ultimately set or clear billing-related exceptions automatically.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="build-standard" data-doc>
        <h2>Production Website Build Standard</h2>
        <ul><li>Use reusable CajunSites templates and shared components instead of bespoke architecture for every customer.</li><li>Drive sites with customer-specific configuration and approved content.</li><li>Use customer-provided or otherwise verified facts only.</li><li>Mobile-first and responsive on common widths.</li><li>Keep navigation simple and conversion-oriented.</li><li>Use accessible semantic structure, readable contrast, useful alt text, and usable forms.</li><li>Preserve customer ownership of their domain.</li><li>Final production imagery/content must be customer-approved.</li></ul>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="seo" data-doc>
        <h2>Local SEO Foundation Standard</h2>
        <p>Customer-facing wording: <strong>Local SEO Foundation Included</strong> or <strong>Search-engine optimized from day one.</strong></p>
        <p>Included: real service/location keyword targeting, unique titles/meta, logical headings, natural location references, alt text, clean URLs, internal links, mobile/performance optimization, HTTPS, sitemap, robots.txt, appropriate schema, Search Console verification/submission when applicable, and GBP linking when available.</p>
        <p>Not included: ranking guarantees, paid link building, spam city pages, monthly SEO content, ongoing GBP management, or an ongoing SEO campaign under the $49/month plan.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="maintenance" data-doc>
        <h2>Hosting & Maintenance Standard</h2>
        <table><thead><tr><th>Request</th><th>Treatment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Routine update to existing text, image, phone, hours, or services</td><td>Included</td></tr><tr><td>Repair caused by CajunSites platform or implementation</td><td>Included</td></tr><tr><td>New page, feature, major redesign, integration, or custom project</td><td>Quote separately</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="architecture" data-doc>
        <h2>Technical Architecture</h2>
        <table><thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Platform</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Registrar, DNS, CDN, SSL, Worker runtime, D1</td><td>Cloudflare</td></tr><tr><td>Static site framework</td><td>Astro</td></tr><tr><td>Source control / CI</td><td>GitHub</td></tr><tr><td>Payments/subscriptions</td><td>Stripe</td></tr><tr><td>Customer transactional email</td><td>Resend</td></tr><tr><td>Lead/onboarding internal email</td><td>Cloudflare Email Service</td></tr><tr><td>Form abuse protection</td><td>Cloudflare Turnstile</td></tr><tr><td>Business research</td><td>OpenAI + web search</td></tr><tr><td>Prospect concept hosting</td><td>Vercel</td></tr><tr><td>Internal operational data</td><td>Cloudflare D1</td></tr><tr><td>Bookkeeping</td><td>Zoho Books Free</td></tr></tbody></table>
        <h3>Current Worker Route Chain</h3><p><code>prospect-cleanup → vertical-concepts → conversion → concept-factory → prospects → auth → app → index</code></p>
        <p>This wrapper chain should be consolidated into one top-level router with focused service modules as the product matures.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="payments" data-doc>
        <h2>Payments & Billing</h2>
        <ul><li>$499 Website Design & Launch, one time.</li><li>$49 Hosting & Maintenance, monthly recurring.</li><li>Standard checkout currently charges $548 at purchase, then $49/month.</li><li>Stripe terms acceptance is required.</li><li>Stripe Tax remains disabled pending final tax treatment review.</li><li>Dashboard revenue figures that multiply customer count by standard pricing are model estimates, not authoritative Stripe accounting.</li></ul>
        <div class="callout">Next billing improvement: synchronize recurring payment health, cancellations, refunds, and recovery events into customer status and analytics.</div>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="onboarding" data-doc>
        <h2>Onboarding Automation</h2>
        <p>Successful paid Stripe checkout creates/loads the D1 customer, sends the welcome email, and generates a signed customer-specific onboarding URL. The onboarding submission verifies the signed link, stores the intake payload, and moves the customer from Paid - Awaiting Onboarding to Onboarding Received.</p>
        <div class="callout">Never direct a paid customer to the generic onboarding URL. Use the signed welcome-email link.</div>
        <h3>Improvement Direction</h3><ul><li>Use a dedicated onboarding signing secret rather than coupling onboarding signatures to the Stripe webhook secret.</li><li>Add a controlled link reissue/expiration model.</li><li>Consider secure direct upload for logos/photos instead of relying only on shared links.</li></ul>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="dashboard" data-doc>
        <h2>Dashboard Operations</h2>
        <p>The dashboard uses individual internal accounts, role-based API authorization, server-side sessions, secure HttpOnly cookies, and client-rendered data views.</p>
        <h3>Areas</h3><ul><li>Overview: priority customer work, workload, MRR estimate, recent activity</li><li>Prospects: qualification, research, concept builds, outreach, conversion</li><li>Customers: paid customer/onboarding/lifecycle detail</li><li>Onboarding: intake review and readiness</li><li>Build Queue: fulfillment workflow</li><li>Sites: preview/production/domain/template metadata</li><li>Activity: operational audit history</li><li>Templates: standardized production foundations</li><li>Analytics: current modeled business performance</li><li>Documentation: standards/runbooks</li><li>Internal Users: owner-managed access</li><li>Settings: configuration summary</li></ul>
        <h3>Dashboard Improvement Direction</h3><ul><li>Add prospect follow-up/build/research exceptions to Overview.</li><li>Add prospect conversion and fulfillment cycle-time analytics.</li><li>Replace static Configured badges with a protected health endpoint.</li><li>Use Stripe-backed financial metrics.</li><li>Format timestamps for the operator.</li><li>Replace silent client-side catches with visible error/retry states.</li><li>Add a mobile-visible Sign Out control because the desktop topbar is hidden on small screens.</li></ul>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="security" data-doc>
        <h2>Security & Data Handling</h2>
        <ul><li>Store production secrets in Cloudflare runtime secrets, never source control.</li><li>Stripe webhook requests require HMAC verification and timestamp tolerance.</li><li>Turnstile protects public lead and onboarding forms.</li><li>Admin API requests require authenticated sessions and role checks.</li><li>Admin session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure, and SameSite=Strict.</li><li>Dashboard pages are marked noindex/nofollow, but that is not access control.</li><li>Protect <code>/admin/*</code> at the server or Cloudflare Access layer before treating dashboard page content itself as private.</li><li>Limit stored customer data to what is needed to build and support the site.</li></ul>
        <h3>Internal Password Compatibility</h3><p>The login path currently accepts both the HMAC records used by the existing login/bootstrap path and PBKDF2 records created by the original Add User/Reset Password path. This compatibility closes the immediate unusable-password gap, but the target state is one explicitly versioned password scheme with a dedicated pepper.</p>
        <h3>Repository Visibility</h3><p>The current GitHub repository is public. Even without committed secret values, a public repo exposes implementation details and operational identifiers. Consider making it private as customer volume increases.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="database" data-doc>
        <h2>Database & Migration Standard</h2>
        <p>Tracked D1 migrations currently begin with <code>0002_admin_dashboard.sql</code>. A canonical <code>0001</code> for the original customers schema is still needed for clean-environment reproducibility.</p>
        <ul><li>Add a tracked migration for research fields.</li><li>Move request-time CREATE/ALTER operations into explicit migrations.</li><li>Move prospect seed records out of schema migrations/runtime auto-seeding and into an explicit bootstrap/dev seed process.</li><li>Define intended foreign-key behavior for prospect/customer linkage where practical.</li><li>Do not silently recreate sales prospects when the production pipeline is intentionally empty.</li></ul>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="deployment" data-doc>
        <h2>Deployment & CI Runbook</h2>
        <ol><li>Make and review the source change.</li><li>CI validates Worker JavaScript syntax.</li><li>CI builds the Astro site.</li><li>Confirm production deployment completes.</li><li>Verify the changed public/dashboard page.</li><li>For Worker changes, exercise the relevant endpoint with controlled test data.</li><li>For database features, apply/verify the tracked migration.</li><li>Do not use a real customer/payment for destructive or billing tests unless explicitly intended.</li></ol>
        <h3>Next CI Additions</h3><p>Wrangler bundle/dry-run validation plus unit tests for vertical classification, status transitions, authentication hash compatibility, onboarding signing, prospect cleanup, and webhook conversion retry/idempotency.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="qa" data-doc>
        <h2>Internal Website QA Checklist</h2>
        <ul><li>Business name/contact information correct</li><li>No invented claims or unsupported credentials</li><li>All required pages/sections present</li><li>Navigation and CTAs work</li><li>Contact/quote form works end to end</li><li>Phone/email links work</li><li>Mobile layout checked</li><li>No overflow/clipped content</li><li>Images load, match the business category, and do not imply false ownership</li><li>Title/meta/H1 reviewed</li><li>Canonical/robots/sitemap appropriate</li><li>Structured data uses true facts only</li><li>HTTPS active</li><li>Preview approved before production cutover</li><li>Production domain validated after launch</li></ul>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="incident" data-doc>
        <h2>Incident & Recovery</h2>
        <h3>Concept Build Failure</h3><ol><li>Review research/build error and Activity.</li><li>Confirm Vercel and DNS integration health.</li><li>Verify the selected visual family and external imagery.</li><li>Retry only after identifying whether failure occurred before or after DNS/domain creation.</li><li>Clean orphaned assets if a partial deployment occurred.</li></ol>
        <h3>Payment / Conversion Issue</h3><ol><li>Confirm Stripe payment/event state.</li><li>Confirm customer row exists in D1.</li><li>Check source prospect linkage and Won status.</li><li>Review Worker logs before manual data edits.</li><li>Use a reconciliation procedure rather than creating duplicate customer records.</li></ol>
        <h3>Customer Site Issue</h3><ol><li>Identify content, DNS, platform, form, or external dependency.</li><li>Check public site and deployment state.</li><li>Confirm DNS/SSL.</li><li>Review recent deployment/activity history.</li><li>Restore/redeploy last known-good version when appropriate.</li><li>Document the action.</li></ol>
      </article>

      <article class="admin-card doc" id="legal" data-doc>
        <h2>Legal, Domain, Email & Tax Notes</h2>
        <ul><li>Terms: <code>https://cajunsites.com/terms/</code></li><li>Privacy: <code>https://cajunsites.com/privacy/</code></li><li>The customer owns its domain. Do not intentionally create domain lock-in.</li><li>CajunSites does not offer/administer customer business email in the standard service.</li><li>No SEO, traffic, ranking, or business-result guarantees.</li><li>Stripe Tax is currently disabled pending final tax treatment confirmation.</li></ul>
        <div class="callout">Internal documentation is operational guidance and does not replace attorney or CPA review.</div>
      </article>
    </section>
  </div>
</AdminShell>

<script is:inline>
const input=document.getElementById('docSearch');
const docs=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-doc]')];
input?.addEventListener('input',()=>{const q=input.value.trim().toLowerCase();docs.forEach(d=>{d.style.display=!q||d.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q)?'block':'none'})});
</script>
